---
id: org.dxos.plugin.bookmarks
name: BookmarksPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Manages a list of clipped web pages. Bookmarks are created primarily via the
Composer browser extension's "Add bookmark" page action: the extension captures
a snapshot of the current page (title, URL, og metadata, selection) and this
plugin materializes it as a `Bookmark` object in the active space, with a link
back to the original page. Bookmarks render with existing UI components (card
and article surfaces) and can later be enriched with an AI-generated summary
(best-effort, not load-bearing for creation).

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term   | URI                            |
|--------|--------------------------------|
| `type` | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat` | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `test` | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `flow` | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`        |

## Types

```mdl
type Bookmark
  desc: |
    A saved web page. All optional fields are best-effort: a bookmark is
    created even when the page exposes no metadata.
  fields:
    title: string                # hints.ogTitle ?? source.title
    url: string                  # the bookmarked page URL
    favicon?: string             # source.favicon
    image?: string               # imageData (extension-captured thumbnail data URL) ?? hints.ogImage
    excerpt?: string             # hints.ogDescription ?? first 280 chars of selection text
    summary?: Ref<Text>          # generated summary (AI), via Summarize
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Bookmark Schema

  req F-1.1:
    when: plugin is activated
    then: the Bookmark ECHO type is registered with the schema module

  req F-1.2:
    when: a Bookmark is rendered anywhere typed labels are used
    then: its label is the `title` field and its icon is the bookmark icon
```

```mdl
feat F-2: AddFromSnapshot Operation

  req F-2.1:
    when: the operation is invoked with { snapshot, target }
    then: |
      a Bookmark is created in the target database with best-effort fields:
        title     ← snapshot.hints.ogTitle ?? snapshot.source.title
        url       ← snapshot.source.url
        favicon   ← snapshot.source.favicon
        image     ← snapshot.imageData ?? snapshot.hints.ogImage
                    (imageData is the extension-captured thumbnail data URL)
        excerpt   ← snapshot.hints.ogDescription ?? first 280 chars of selection.text
      and the operation returns { id } of the created object.

  req F-2.2:
    when: the snapshot carries no hints and no selection
    then: the Bookmark is still created (title falls back to the tab title)
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Page Action Contribution

  req F-3.1:
    when: plugin is activated
    then: |
      a page action "Add bookmark" is contributed under the plugin-crx
      PageAction capability with:
        urlPatterns: all http(s) URLs
        extractor:   snapshot
        contexts:    popup, page
        operation:   AddFromSnapshot

  req F-3.2:
    when: the browser extension lists page actions
    then: the action appears in the extension popup on any http(s) page
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Surfaces

  req F-4.1:
    when: a Bookmark is the subject of an article surface
    then: |
      a panel renders the title, image (when present), excerpt, summary
      (when present), and a button that opens the source URL in a new tab

  req F-4.2:
    when: a Bookmark is the subject of a card surface
    then: a card renders the title, excerpt, and image (when present)

  req F-4.3:
    when: the article toolbar is rendered
    then: |
      it uses the standard menu toolbar (MenuBuilder) with two actions:
        open-source: opens the bookmarked URL in a new tab (disabled when
                     the URL is not a valid http(s) URL)
        summarize:   invokes the Summarize operation (disabled while a
                     summarization is already running)
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Summarize Operation

  req F-5.1:
    when: the operation is invoked with { bookmark }
    then: |
      the bookmarked page's HTML is fetched via the Composer extension's
      render-proxy (falling back to the EDGE CORS proxy when the extension
      is unavailable), readable text is extracted from the HTML, a markdown
      summary is generated via the assistant AI stack and stored as a linked
      Text object, and the operation returns { summary } (a Ref to the
      created Text object).

  req F-5.2:
    when: the summary Text object is created
    then: the bookmark's `summary` field references it and the article
          surface renders its markdown content

  req F-5.3:
    when: the fetch, extraction, or generation fails
    then: the failure surfaces as an error toast and the bookmark is left
          unmodified
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Comments

  req F-6.1:
    when: a Bookmark is the active subject
    then: |
      the comments companion is offered (via the comments plugin's
      CommentConfig capability, comments: unanchored); comment threads
      attach to the bookmark as a whole.

  req F-6.2:
    note: |
      Anchored (text-range) comments into Bookmark.summary require the
      comment-sync editor extension, which currently only targets
      Markdown.Document content. Follow-up.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Snapshot mapping prefers og hints
  given: a snapshot with ogTitle, ogDescription, ogImage, favicon, clippedAt
  when: Bookmark.fromSnapshot is applied
  then:
    - title === ogTitle
    - excerpt === ogDescription
    - image === ogImage
    - favicon === source.favicon
```

```mdl
test T-2: Snapshot mapping falls back without hints
  given: a snapshot with no hints and a long text selection
  when: Bookmark.fromSnapshot is applied
  then:
    - title === source.title (the tab title)
    - excerpt is the first 280 characters of the selection text
    - image is unset
```

```mdl
test T-3: AddFromSnapshot persists a Bookmark
  given: an in-memory database
  when: AddFromSnapshot is invoked with { snapshot, target }
  then:
    - a Bookmark object exists in the database
    - the operation returns the object's id
```

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Save a bookmark and summarize it
  desc: The core round-trip — capture a page snapshot as a Bookmark, then generate its AI summary.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-5.1, F-5.2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - no Bookmark with url "https://example.com/qa-notes" exists — ABORT rather than deleting
      one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Add a bookmark from a captured snapshot
      do: |
        On https://example.com/qa-notes, open the Composer browser extension popup and click
        "Add bookmark". The extension captures title, url, og metadata and any selection and
        invokes the operation on the active space.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.bookmarks.addFromSnapshot {
          snapshot: { source: { url: "https://example.com/qa-notes", title: "QA Notes", clippedAt: "2026-08-27T00:00:00Z" }, hints: { ogTitle: "QA Notes Page" } },
          target: $given.space.db
        }
      capture: created
      expect: a Bookmark titled "QA Notes Page" now exists with url "https://example.com/qa-notes"
      assert: return !!$created.id
      note: |
        `target` is the database itself, not a collection — AddFromSnapshot writes directly and
        has no separate placement step, unlike a navtree-created object.
    - name: Summarize the bookmark
      do: Open the bookmark and click "Summarize" in the article toolbar.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.bookmarks.summarize { bookmark: { "/": "echo://$given.space.id/$created.id" } }
      expect: the article surface now renders a generated markdown summary
      assert: return !!$result.summary
  after:
    - name: Delete the bookmark
      do: Right-click the bookmark card and choose Delete.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [{ "/": "echo://$given.space.id/$created.id" }], target: $given.space.db }
      expect: the bookmark no longer appears in the space
```

```mdl
flow QA-2: Page action is contributed to the extension
  desc: The plugin-crx integration surface — no operation invokes this, it is a registration check.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-3.1, F-3.2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - the Composer browser extension is installed and pointed at this space
    - a normal http(s) page is open in the browser
  test:
    - name: Open the extension popup
      do: Click the Composer extension icon in the browser toolbar.
      expect: the popup lists "Add bookmark" among the available page actions
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — this checks the extension's own popup UI, not an ECHO effect; there is
        nothing in the database to assert against until the action is actually run (QA-1).
```

